{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:7b82ea59e406f74a","name":"Loose Sand","source":{"id":"source:reference-7b82ea59e406f74a","title":"Loose Sand","revision":21368,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:40:18Z","sha256":"76d9ab2882c260e9670dc389b5e48b18dd3fd254a6ac9273385b0b15b39734b0","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21368","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Loose%20Sand&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-7b82ea59e406f74a","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unknown Regions Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unknown_Regions_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["The sand beneath your feet shifts as you move, making progress difficult."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Technically, all sand in a desert is loose, but some areas are less tightly packed than others. Creatures unfortunate enough to stand in such an area have a hard time moving out of it. Placing Loose Sand atop a dune or in the middle of a dry riverbed could put the heroes in a position where they have little or no cover against enemies that find them.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Loose Sand Statistics (CL 1)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Keywords:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Natural"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Natural"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trigger:"]}," A being begins its turn on Loose Sand.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Attack:"]}," +3 vs ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 2d8+1 (See Below)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Recurrence:"]}," Each round at the start of the target's turn, as long as the target remains on the Loose Sand.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"},":"]}," The following are suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"}," for this Hazard:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Acrobatics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Acrobatics","referenceId":"reference:0d0b7eee2953750e"}," (DC 18):"]}," The character tumbles through the sand to reach more stable ground, gaining a +2 circumstance bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," against the Hazard."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Jump"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jump","referenceId":"reference:9ee0ca3e24d60ea0"}," (DC 23):"]}," The character attempts to leap out of the Loose Sand, gaining a +5 circumstance bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," against the Hazard."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knowledge (Physical Sciences)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knowledge_(Physical_Sciences)"}," (DC 13):"]}," The character notices that the sand appears loose."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special:"]}," If the Hazard's attack is successful, the target is restricted to one ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"}," per round, but the target cannot leave its square because it is unable to find secure footing. If the Hazard's attack fails, the target can leave its square.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
